WEBVTT

00:40:27.606 --> 00:40:31.666
So, we face a common set of problems:
World War II, The Depression, whatever.

00:40:31.690 --> 00:40:34.432
We create a culture to fix it
and we do that collectively,

00:40:34.456 --> 00:40:36.320
and we ratchet upward, we move upward,

00:40:36.344 --> 00:40:38.753
and that culture works for a while.

00:40:38.777 --> 00:40:40.808
And then it stops working.

00:40:40.832 --> 00:40:43.655
And then you have to hatchet it up,
you have to chop it up.

00:40:43.679 --> 00:40:47.808
And those are moments of paradigm shift,
when everything is in uproar.

00:40:47.832 --> 00:40:51.140
And 1968 was such a moment,
1848 was such a moment,

00:40:51.164 --> 00:40:53.535
probably 1905, and now is such a moment.

00:40:53.559 --> 00:40:54.883
We're chopping it all up.

00:40:54.907 --> 00:40:57.839
And in those moments when
you're chopping up the old paradigm,

00:40:57.863 --> 00:40:59.138
it can seem really messy.

00:40:59.162 --> 00:41:03.184
But I have faith in human ingenuity
that we'll figure it out,